  "maintenanceProfileConfirm": "Delete the saved profile template, including its name and avatar. Copies in the local group and existing games, and online profiles, remain. Continue?",
  "maintenanceGamesConfirm": "End both local games and remove them from the saved state and recovery copies. Keep the profile template, group and six-hour draw history. This does not leave or close online rooms. Continue?",
  "maintenanceProfileDeleted": "The profile template was deleted.",
  "maintenanceGamesDeleted": "Local games were also removed from recovery copies. Draw history is retained.",
  "maintenanceFailed": "Deletion could not be fully confirmed. Saved data may still remain. Please try again.",
  "helpCardsTitle": "Phone + physical cards",
  "helpCardsBody": "For 3–20 people, with no required profiles: choose player count, cases, rules and factor. The default is 50 cases and seven rules. Read the question and scale and deal real number cards to everyone except the judge. Order and judge at the table. Next counts the played case without inventing an error or sip score in the app.",
  "helpSharedTitle": "One shared phone",
  "helpSharedBody": "Set up the group and seat order. After the case file, pass the phone to the displayed person, who confirms their name and seat. The number appears only while holding the reveal area. Releasing hides it. Done passes to the next person; finally the judge confirms the return. Interruptions require confirmation again and never advance automatically.",
  "helpOnlineTitle": "A phone for everyone",
  "helpOnlineBody": "With a configured server, the host creates a room and others join using its code or invitation link. A link only fills the code. Edit your profile in Me; play in Courtroom. Each eligible person explicitly reveals and confirms their own number. Readiness and order wait for server confirmation. After a connection loss, resume the same saved identity.",
  "helpVerdictTitle": "Verdict and sips",
  "helpVerdictBody": "Normal: for E wrong positions, the judge and each wrongly placed person drink E sips each; correctly placed people drink none. All are judges: everyone submits their own order and drinks only for errors in that order. There are no extra sips for someone else’s errors. Digital verdicts come from the game core or server.",
  "helpRefreshTitle": "New question, same case",
  "helpRefreshBody": "Refresh on the left of the case file replaces the question before the first public reveal. Case number, roles, numbers and rule schedule remain; digital confirmations and orders restart. Online, only the current judge, or the reader when all are judges, may refresh. Every shown question counts as drawn. When no replacement remains, the current question stays and a message explains why.",
  "helpPeopleTitle": "Group, numbers and seating",
  "helpPeopleBody": "The scale runs from 1 to player count times the factor (1.0–3.0), rounded up. Follow numbered snake seats: 1→2→3, then 6←5←4. Drag, tap a person and target, use arrow buttons or Alt + Up/Down to insert instead of swapping. Roster changes apply at the next case boundary; current roles and numbers stay assigned.",
  "helpOfflineTitle": "Offline readiness",
  "helpOfflineBody": "Android bundles local game content. On the web, wait for the full offline download in Settings and check its confirmed readiness status. Private mode, quota limits or cleared browser storage can prevent resume. Cache updates and removal wait while a local game is active. Online rooms require a connection. Audio is optional and never required for play.",
  "helpResumeTitle": "Restart, deletion and room lifetime",
  "helpResumeBody": "Returning to selection keeps a local game. A confirmed restart discards its progress and keeps the profile and six-hour draw history. Delete games and the profile template separately in Settings. Online rooms expire after 24 hours without real game activity, at most 48 hours after creation. Leaving revokes your identity; only the host can close the room. Forgetting locally is not a confirmed server revocation.",
  "helpTroubleshootingTitle": "When something goes wrong",
  "helpTroubleshootingBody": "Use the displayed retry action for loading or storage errors. For reconnect, select the saved identity instead of inventing a second player. A valid backup may recover a damaged local game; confirmed deletion also sanitizes game copies. For bug reports, record app version, mode and error message only. Do not share secret numbers, room tokens, storage files or private network payloads.",
  "privacyLocalTitle": "What is stored locally",
  "privacyLocalBody": "This device stores the name and avatar template, local group, language and preferences. Local games contain roles, numbers, orders, rules and progress, with a recovery copy. Shared-device game data exists on the device even when the UI hides numbers. Hiding is not protection against someone controlling device storage or a debugger.",
  "privacyOnlineTitle": "Data used in online play",
  "privacyOnlineBody": "Creating, joining or resuming sends the profile, room/game identifiers and necessary game actions to the configured server. It processes numbers, orders, readiness, verdicts and bounded draw/retry data. Private numbers and personal orders are projected only for the appropriate identity and phase. Spoken answers are not entered or archived as answer text.",
  "privacyCredentialsTitle": "Saved room identities",
  "privacyCredentialsBody": "There are no user accounts. A random resume token binds room identity to this installation. Android uses the secure-storage plugin; the web uses origin-bound IndexedDB. Anyone gaining access to that identity can use it. Invitation links contain only the public room code, never the resume token.",
  "privacyRetentionTitle": "Retention and expiry",
  "privacyRetentionBody": "Local draw history covers six hours and contains content/event identifiers and timestamps. A normal restart does not erase it. Server rooms expire after 24 hours without real game activity, at most 48 hours after creation. Connections and retries alone do not extend these limits. Room closure cleans room state and private game data.",
  "privacyDeletionTitle": "Separate deletion controls",
  "privacyDeletionBody": "Deleting the profile template removes that template, not copies in groups or games. Deleting local games ends both local games and removes recovery copies of them; profile, group and draw history remain. Remove group characters in people management. For online data, leave the room or close it as host; forgetting locally only removes local identity. Failed actions are never reported as confirmed deletion.",
  "privacyOperationsTitle": "Operation and deployment details",
  "privacyOperationsBody": "The app has no account login, advertising or app analytics/answer archive. Online play sends data to the server displayed above; none is assumed without configuration. Before public distribution, add operator/contact and actual hosting details. A local review artifact is not a publicly deployed service.",
